"""Long-form article — Best LED Light Bars & Light Kits for 2019–2026 Chevrolet Silverado 1500 (4th gen, T1).
Mirrors the approved pilot (ford_f150_2021_tonneau.py) and the F-150 / Tacoma / Tundra light-bar pages. No invented
hands-on testing: every spec comes from the maker/retailer pages listed in sources (checked 2026-10-05). Bars are
mostly universal; what is Silverado-specific is the mount (behind the grille, top of the bumper, hood hinge / lower
windshield, roof) and the 2019–2021 vs 2022+ front-end split. Baja Designs' fit list is the source for that split
(grille kit 2019–21, fog pocket kit 2019–22, A-pillar kit 2019–2026). Chevrolet's media site blocked our fetch, so the
refresh is described from Wikipedia and the trim-level detail is left to the owner's manual and the listing. Rough
Country's and ZROADZ's own product pages could not be opened, so those picks are described from listing titles plus
RealTruck's ZROADZ family pages, and the text says so. No fog-pocket listing with a model year in its title was found,
so fog pocket kits are covered as a "confirm" option, not a pick. Upfitter switches: no Chevrolet source found, so
the page says we could not confirm.
"""

