FAQ = [
 ("What is the best LED light bar for a 2019–2026 Silverado 1500?",
  "For a 2019–2021 truck, Baja Designs' S8 20 in grille light bar kit. Baja lists it for the 2019–2021 Silverado 1500 at 12,700 lumens, 120 watts and 8.0 amps, rated IP69K, with stainless brackets that fit factory locations without cutting or trimming, and it says the kit is not compatible with LTZ models. Baja lists it at $862.95 with a limited lifetime warranty. For a 2022–2026 truck, no grille kit we found names the refreshed front end, so the ditch light kits that run through 2024 or 2026 are the safer first buy."),
 ("Do 2019–2021 Silverado light bar brackets fit a 2022 or newer Silverado?",
  "Not always, and the maker fit lists are the only reliable guide. Wikipedia says the refreshed 2022 Silverado 1500 received a new front-end design. Baja Designs lists its S8 grille kit for 2019–2021 only and its Squadron SAE fog pocket kit for 2019–2022, but its Squadron 2.0 A-pillar kits for 2019–2026. In short, grille and fog mounts changed with the front end, while hood-hinge and A-pillar mounts carry across. The 2022 Silverado 1500 LTD is the pre-refresh truck, so 2019–2021 front-end kits are the ones to check for it. Buy a listing that names your model year."),
 ("Does the Silverado 1500 have factory upfitter or auxiliary switches?",
  "We could not confirm from a Chevrolet source that any 2019–2026 Silverado 1500 trim ships with factory auxiliary switches, so don't plan on them. Check your owner's manual and the overhead console and dash blanks on your truck. Every complete kit on this page includes its own harness and switch, or is sold with one as an option, and the bracket-only picks need a relay harness with an inline fuse and a switch. If your truck does have an auxiliary switch bank, ask the kit maker how to connect to it before cutting into the supplied harness."),
 ("Are LED light bars legal on the road in a Silverado?",
  "Usually not while driving. KC HiLiTES says that in general it is illegal to have off-road-only lights turned on while on the roadway, that California requires them covered with an opaque cover and turned off, and that Pennsylvania requires roof-mounted off-road lights covered on the highway. KC also notes states that cap the number of front lamps, and gives typical mounting heights of 16 to 42 in for driving lights and 12 to 30 in for fog lights. Grille, bumper, ditch and roof bars on this page are off-road lights. Fog pocket kits built to SAE J583 are the street-friendly exception. Check your own state's law."),
 ("Which mount is best for a Silverado: grille, bumper, ditch or roof?",
  "Grille for a hidden bar with the least glare, bumper top for a bigger bar that still sits low, ditch for trail edges and corners, roof for maximum reach. Baja's S8 sits behind the grille at 12,700 lumens and keeps the stock look. ZROADZ's bumper-top kit carries a 30 in curved double-row bar above the bumper. Ditch kits from Rough Country and ZROADZ put two 2 or 3 in pods at the lower windshield or hood hinges. The ZROADZ roof kit carries a 50 in curved bar, which lights farthest but adds wind noise and the most hood glare. Most owners start with a grille bar or ditch pods."),
 ("Will a Silverado grille light bar fit a GMC Sierra 1500?",
  "Don't assume it. The 2019+ Silverado and Sierra 1500 share the cab and bed, but Wikipedia notes the Sierra differentiates itself with its own features, and the grille and bumper kits on this page name the Silverado only. The hood-hinge ditch brackets are the exception: ROMELACK's 2022–2026 brackets name both the Silverado and the Sierra 1500 in their title. For a grille, bumper-top or roof kit on a Sierra, buy a listing that names the Sierra, or ask the seller with your VIN."),
 ("Do I need to drill to install a light bar on a Silverado?",
  "Not for most mounts here. Baja says its S8 grille brackets fit into factory locations without cutting or trimming. RealTruck describes ZROADZ's hood hinge mounts as 100 percent bolt-on with no drilling or cutting, and its 30 in curved top-bumper bar as an easy bolt-on install. Rough Country's ditch kit title says lower windshield, but we could not open Rough Country's install sheet, so confirm the mounting method on the listing. The roof kit is the one to read carefully: confirm on the listing whether the ZROADZ roof brackets bolt to existing points or need holes. Wiring is where you may need to pass a harness through the firewall."),
 ("How much current does a Silverado light bar draw?",
  "Baja lists the S8 20 in grille bar at 120 watts and 8.0 amps. Baja's Squadron SAE fog pocket lights are 29 watts each, so a pair draws roughly 4.2 amps at 13.8 volts. Rough Country and ZROADZ don't publish watts for the kits here on pages we could read, so check the listing and divide watts by about 13.8 to estimate amps. A 50 in double-row roof bar can draw far more than a pair of pods. Every bar or pair of pods needs a relay, an inline fuse sized for the load and a switch, and a long roof-bar run needs heavier wire than a pod harness."),
 ("Can I add street-legal fog lights to a Silverado instead of a bar?",
  "Yes. Baja Designs lists its Chevy Squadron SAE fog pocket light kit, SKU 447528, for the 2019–2022 Silverado 1500 at $554.95. Baja says the lights are designed to meet the current SAE J583 fog lamp requirements, lists 2,420 lumens and 29 watts per light, and includes wire adapters that plug into the OEM connectors and brackets that retain the stock mounting points, with a limited lifetime warranty. We did not find an Amazon listing for it whose title names a Silverado model year, so buy it from Baja or confirm the year on whatever listing you use. Baja's fit list stops at 2022, so 2023–2026 owners should ask Baja first."),
 ("What should Trail Boss and ZR2 owners check before buying a Silverado light kit?",
  "The trim notes on the listing. Chevrolet says the Custom Trail Boss, LT Trail Boss and ZR2 carry a 2 in factory lift, which raises every mount, and the ZR2 arrived for 2022, the refresh year. We could not confirm from a maker fit list which trims use a different front bumper, so we don't claim one here. What we can say is that Baja excludes the LTZ from its S8 grille kit, and that none of the listings here name the Trail Boss or ZR2 by name. Before you order a grille or bumper-top kit for either trim, send the seller your VIN and a photo of the front end."),
]

